From: Filippo Falezza <filippo.falezza@outlook.it>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 16:28:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 15/69] phy: qcom: qmp-ufs: Add SM7250 support

The SM7250 (lito) UFS PHY does not match any existing table set: its COM
block is QMP v4, its RX lanes use the v5 layout, and its TX lanes place the
PWM gear dividers at 0x168-0x174 (0x10 below the v5 layout). Add dedicated
tables, generated from the downstream phy-qcom-ufs-qmp-v4-lito.h (rate A
"no_g4" table plus the second-lane table; lane 1 was verified to mirror
lane 0), and limit the PHY to HS-G3 as downstream does. Regulator loads
come from the downstream devicetree.

Tested on nairo with linux-next 20261002 plus the SM7250 v9 series ("Add
support for SM7250", patches 03/04/09/10/11/12). The link comes up and
all six LUNs of the Samsung KM2V8001CM-B707 enumerate. It currently
negotiates HS-G1 rate B only; HS-G3 is not verified yet.

This patch was generated by an AI coding assistant (Claude Opus 5.5 in
Claude Code) during an interactive bring-up session on a Motorola Moto G
5G Plus (XT2075-3, "nairo"). It has not yet been reviewed line by line
by a human and needs that review before any submission.

Assisted-by: LLM
